think ALES162 and ALES163 carried the gate and limiter into stereo over time; this rung takes the last of the three mechanical siblings ALES161 opened — the attack/release downward expander carried into stereo — and with it the stereo time-varying dynamics quartet (compress/gate/limit/expand over one linked envelope) is whole, exactly as the memoryless quartet closed at ALES159. The mono family crossed this seam at ALES61, spending ALES52's envelope to drive ALES60's deepened floor so a note's tail falls smoothly.
think The shape spends both proofs: advance ONE shared envelope toward the linked peak by ALES160's stereo_env_step; at or above the threshold both pass (continuous at the threshold); below it, exp = max(0, thr − deficit·num/den) on the ENVELOPE (ALES60's floor), one gain exp/e to BOTH raw samples. A shared envelope of exactly zero arises only when both channels are silent (asserted), so no divide by zero.
